{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608474-compact-fire-starters","id":608474,"title":"(Compact) Fire Starters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T15:13:34-07:00","id":608474,"title":"(Compact) Fire Starters","content":"A tenement is lit ablaze, and the following day, a massive surge of gang violence breaks out. Before the end of the week, dozens will be dead, including a cop, and the event shall take up the evening news. Why, for example, did so many victims get killed by claws? <br /> <br /> Its a snowy Christmas Eve in the suburbs, all quiet until four homes erupt into flames. That Christmas Day, six men and two women will be gone, little more than ash. In the following weeks, many bodies will be found, some with scorch marks from flames. The police will cover up that some of the victims seem to be drained of blood. <br /> <br /> A high rise condo becomes engulfed in flame, and while some children will survive, corpses of the adults will be found the following day. Then, violence erupts, and engulfs the city like a plague. <br /> <br /> Cities across the world will sometimes be victim to a special type of arson. Investigations are held, but they always end up being distracted by a massive outbreak of violence following the fires. By the time it ends, anyone involved in the arson is long dead. A scapegoat always reveals themselves sooner or later in the process, so that the city can move on. <br /> <br /> The buildings that burn, on the surface, have no real pattern. One year, a neighborhood will be lit ablaze, the next, tenements. Sometimes the fires are started with military grade napalm, secured from who knows where. Sometimes with bottles of gasoline, or even a simple match. But, unbeknownst to the police, or the victims even, they all have the same source. <br /> <br /> Across the world, there is a religion worshipping a deity of flames. Whenever a fire gets to the correct size, is started by human hands, and causes just enough destruction, those who know how to look will see things they shouldn't. The truth of many will be revealed, whether they want it to be or not. Those who cheat their fellows of just rewards for their own profit to those who stalk the night for the blood of the living and everything in between is revealed. All is seen in the blaze. <br /> <br /> Then, so it goes, carnage must follow, enacted against those who have become too comfortable in their lies. This is not for justice, but rather for the continued blessing of this deity of flames. For blood and death must flow as surely as the flames once did, until such a time the deity appears satisfied.<br /> In return for the ceremony, those who performed it successfully are granted something they hold dear to their hearts, and are freed of any negative consequences connected to the blaze. Riches, fame, or even freedom from oppression can all be gained. <br /> <br /> But surely, that's all a myth, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:14:07-07:00","id":609861,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>The Enemy</b><br /> </div> Anyone, including mortals, could be hunted by the Fire Starters. The only unifying themes that they constantly lie to those around them, and that they are supposed to be trustworthy. Whether it is to hide some part about their very existence, to hide illicit sources of income, or for the purposes of mere financial fraud doesn't matter, only that they lied despite being trustworthy. The focus on those supposed to be trustworthy, however, does contain their targets. <br /> <br /> On the supernatural side, Vampires and Werewolves get targeted immensely, for both hide their nature as much as possible from humans. The professions persons work in, however, are the biggest indicator of whom will get targeted. Priests, virtually any sort of law enforcement official, judges, medical professionals, and those working in mental health fields are all common targets. All the jobs share in common that they are supposed to be trustworthy, and in some cases, that society depends on them being trustworthy. <br /> <br /> Buildings are also chosen partially for how many lies they contain. Tenements built below code, houses with hidden costs, banks that frequently give bad loans, secret sweatshops and such are common targets to light ablaze. However, buildings also need to either meet the correct size, or be close to other structures that the fire can easily spread to them. Their deity of flame is only pleased by immense, towering fires that light up the night sky for many miles around. All of this combined makes the choice of structure very important, along with that the initial blaze frequently is started with an extremely hard to put out flame. <br /> <br /> For whatever reason, Fire Starters are frequently targeted by Werewolves, and because of their frequent arson, are considered outright terrorists by most governments. <br /> In the following carnage is when most targets are killed, but also when the supernatural is drawn out. The initial blaze frequently stirs up a hornets nest of supernatural activity that adds to the carnage of the weeks following the initial arson. Strange things, from people that burst into rats, some of the arsonists seeming to shoot fire from their fingers, and even hunters walking around ablaze for hours before being killed, all seem to occur in these weeks of carnage. <br /> <br /> All of this means, when they do start the correct kind of fire, targets will never be in short supply, nor will violence. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:09:41-07:00","id":610016,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>History</b></div> <br /> It all began with a bunch of kids. In revenge for being expelled, among other things, they lit a man's home on fire, wanting to destroy his life like he did theirs. But... the blaze spoke to them. The voice promised that they would never be punished for this act of arson, or any of the crimes that followed, if in return, they killed liars. It also said that, at the end of the ordeal, they would each be granted a single wish. Over the following weeks, they would do as it asked, however only one would survive the ordeal. He asked to be taken to a paradise, and for all that is known, he was. <br /> <br /> True or not, it is known the Fire Starters originate somewhere in the 20th century, and have committed hundreds of acts of arson, and have a body count numbering in the tens of thousands. That they lose the consequences of their actions fits with that, despite efforts of police, among other organizations, there is never any forensic evidence found leading to a person from the organization once the weeks of carnage conclude. That a rather high proportion of these persons die in the process doesn't help matters. <br /> <br /> Most who become a Fire Starter do so very briefly. They are in to get a wish, after all, and since the entire cycle lasts a month at most usually, they are out rapidly, having received what they desired or died trying. The few permanent members are... strange. It is as if they embody flame itself, and can create it from nothing. Such impacts the makeup of the group heavily. <br /> <br /> The Fire Starters continue to survive from having lots of recruits, and spread anywhere that targets are available to burn. The weeks of carnage frequently covers up their presence as either gang violence or some other more mundane outbreak of crime. For the supernatural, they cause such an outbreak of supernatural presence to occur that it covers up their very existence. <br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Factions</b></div> <br /> <b>Arsonists: </b>The classic faction, and still the majority of members. Only in for the reward at the end, and having seen the deity in a prior massive flame. They don't particularly care who they hunt, only that it counts in the eyes of the entity that promises them a prize. They will use fire a lot however, in the hope of gaining continued assurances from the deity in the fames that erupt from molotovs and such. <br /> <br /> <b>Believers: </b>By contrast, the rarest faction, and the one that most often appears... off. They claim to continue for the deity itself, but they always seem to be concealing something, and be capable of more than they let on. However, they also seem to last the longest of any. <br /> <br /> <b>Soldiers</b>: Those hoping to use the entity to help them kill monsters through tracking them, and even gaining wishes that strengthen them in the pursuit. They also seem to be hoping to hunt down certain members, but, this rarely ends well. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:53:36-07:00","id":610047,"title":"","content":"Do Fire Starters have an Endowment? they seems to be patronized by a Fire related Spirit (which would explain why Urathas target the group), so maybe it could act as a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:54:33-07:00","id":610276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608474-compact-fire-starters?p=610047#post610047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fire Starters have an Endowment? they seems to be patronized by a Fire related Spirit (which would explain why Urathas target the group), so maybe it could act as a totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't worked on the Endowement but, they indeed have a Spirit patron. A rather powerful too, as, by working with it, they're actually weakening the Gauntlet, which I think I gave sufficient hints of.<br /> <br /> Because the Uratha need more human enemies.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:57:52-07:00","id":681604,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that they're a compact with no endowments a lot more than a conspiracy. Possibly the higher ups are Ridden, possibly Urged. This is a really neat concept mind if I use in my next session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5871-monkey-d","name":"Monkey D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T21:32:55-07:00","id":681760,"title":"","content":"What's funny to me is that that profession I just posted would either fit very well within this group, or take up the Vigil because of the actions of this compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T18:09:52-07:00","id":700339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkey D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608474-compact-fire-starters?p=681604#post681604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that they're a compact with no endowments a lot more than a conspiracy. Possibly the higher ups are Ridden, possibly Urged. This is a really neat concept mind if I use in my next session?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for ludicrously late answer, but yes, use them! <br /> <br /> <br /> For Flyboy, interesting. But yeah, I do expect this to be a bit of an antagonist Compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}